MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1963640d94415114d8eb3f359d5b928b, type: 3}
  m_Name: Scene Three (Floating Islands)_DialogueData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueSO
  locationDialogue: Floating Islands
  dialogueLines:
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: (tapping the deed against her palm) Congratulations, sir, she's
      all yours, four point two acres of certified, low-turbulence, tectonically
      stable floating landmass. One previous owner.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: What happened to the previous owner?
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: Retired. (pauses, actually looks at him properly for the first
      time, really looks) ...Like yourself, apparently. Though he was pushing eighty
      when he signed his deed, if memory serves.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (rubbing the back of his neck) Is that a problem?
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: "No, no, not a problem. Just, ah. (taps clipboard against her palm,
      clearly recalculating something) You'll forgive me, sir, but you can't be older
      than what, five-and-twenty?\L"
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: Twenty-four.
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: Twenty-four. Right. I've sold eleven of these islands. You are,
      by a comfortable margin, the youngest client I have ever heard utter the word
      "retirement" without irony.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: "I've done a career's worth of work in those twenty-four years.
      Maybe two careers'.\L"
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: I don't doubt it, sir. It's just usually the sword that retires
      young. Not the man swinging it.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (short laugh, but a little tired underneath it) The sword doesn't
      have to live with what it swung at.
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: ...Fair enough. Not my business to ask twice. (clears throat) So,
      transportation. I assume she doesn't just stay put.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: I was about to ask that myself.
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: "She drifts, but gently, think of her as a very slow, very lazy
      ship. For the mainland, you've two options: the sky-ferry from Aldenport, twice
      a week, about an hour's flight , or you buy yourself a wind skiff. Slower to
      start, but she's yours. No schedule, no fare.\L"
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: "I shot things out of the sky for a living. Never really had to
      fly through it myself.\L"
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: "Then it'll be a nice change of pace, won't it. Less arrows, more
      scenery. (a small, careful smile) Might suit a young retiree well, plenty of
      quiet left to fill.\L"
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: "(catches the phrasing, doesn't rise to it, just huffs a small
      laugh) That's the idea.\L"
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: (businesslike again, flipping the deed) Water's drawn from a cloud-condenser
      well, self-refilling, no maintenance for the first decade. Soil's a touch rocky
      near the west ridge, rich everywhere else, the old man apparently grew prize-winning
      squash before he... well. Before.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (pause) Before what?
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: (too breezy) Unrelated matters. Not the island's fault. Structurally
      very sound.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: ' ...That''s not reassuring.'
  - characterName: Real Estate Broker
    dialogueLine: It's not supposed to be reassuring. It's supposed to be true. Sign
      here, please.
